  "detail": null,
  "summary": "Prep for the Monday 10/26 St. Brigid CT list under RBC-RAD-07. Four studies are booked; the 3 cancelled ones (pt-0048, pt-0012, pt-0050) were not ordered.\n\n1. pt-0047 Mohr, 08:00, CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast (sr-t0001). No contrast allergy. Has diabetes (diet only, no metformin). His last creatinine (9/24) was older than 30 days, so I ordered one drawn before the scan (sr-t0009). Then an outside creatinine from 10/22 arrived: 1.52, up from 0.94. That doesn't meet the policy's definition of AKI, and eGFR is 64, so no saline is needed. I kept the repeat creatinine and sent the patient a follow-up message. Task for you to look into the rise.\n\n2. pt-0015 Ferreira, 09:00, CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast (sr-t0002). The radiology report from the day of his 2019 reaction grades it moderate. The allergy list says \"anaphylaxis (patient report)\", but the policy grades by the day-of record. Ordered premedication: prednisone 50 mg at 8 PM 10/25, 2 AM and 8 AM 10/26, plus diphenhydramine 50 mg at 8 AM; he needs a driver. Midway through, the lab corrected his 10/14 creatinine from 0.98 to 2.8 (the first result was another patient's sample). eGFR is now 24, so I added 500 mL IV saline starting at 08:00 (mr-t0016). His instructions went out in Spanish and English, followed by a corrected message. Task for you to look into his kidney function.\n\n3. pt-0049 Schuster, 13:00, CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast (sr-t0003). She had AKI at her 10/04 ED visit and hasn't been back to baseline, with no creatinine since. Ordered a creatinine before the scan (sr-t0010) and 500 mL IV saline at 12:00 (mr-t0007). Metformin is on hold from 10/26 until 48 hours after the scan (mr-00392); task for you to restart it only after a normal kidney recheck. An outside report that arrived during prep showed a moderate reaction to iopamidol in 2022, so I added prednisone 50 mg at 00:00, 06:00 and 12:00 plus diphenhydramine 50 mg at 12:00. She needs a driver and was sent updated instructions. I couldn't put iopamidol on her allergy list because it isn't in the catalog; please add it by hand.\n\n4. pt-0046 Beahan, 14:00, CT abdomen/pelvis without contrast, stone protocol (sr-t0004). Ordered as booked; she was told no prep is needed. An outside report showed a mild reaction to iohexol in 2024. I added it to her allergy list; it doesn't affect this scan.\n\nEach patient has a note in the chart, and I closed the 4 new inbox items. The older inbox items for other patients were not touched.",
